  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Sten Esaias Tegnér was a Swedish businessman whose working life extended across the Atlantic. He owned and operated an American electronics company and a hotel, having spent a decade in the United States before moving to London. His public roles included chairing the Friends of the Nordic Museum and Skansen.",
